## Built: Cadence Studio

I updated the Django project with an original music-studio interface inspired by the features requested, rather than copying Suno’s branded UI. The workspace includes a prompt composer with style tags, BPM/key/length and instrumental controls, a multitrack arrangement, track import and arrangement controls, a creative-refinement panel, and project saving.

The saved-project sidebar now loads the signed-in user’s projects and opens them; edits update the current project. For guests, the current session saves in the browser. I also fixed BPM stepper persistence and made sure a saved prompt without an audio provider is **not** shown as a generated song or playable track.

The requested inspection has limits: Suno redirected the browser to sign-in, so I could inspect the sign-in screen but not its authenticated create experience. REA analysis tools were not available in this session, and Ghidra does not apply to inspecting a live website without a supplied binary. No third-party music-generation API was recommended by the service lookup; consequently, this implementation saves prompts and studio projects but **does not generate music audio**. Playback controls operate the visual timeline, not an audio engine.

**Verification:** Django system check passed, all 5 `studioapp` tests passed, and `node --check` passed. I opened the local page and exercised UI controls including BPM, play/stop, add track, zoom, collapse, refinement and the guest generation/account prompt; no browser console errors were reported. The server-rendered page and its CSS/JS endpoints returned HTTP 200.

Files: [studio template](templates/studio.html), [studio interactions](static/studio.js), [studio styles](static/studio.css), [project README](README.md).

One follow-up could be connecting a licensed music-generation provider so prompts produce playable audio. Another could be adding more timeline editing and playback behavior.
